=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR0004

GOFASTR0004  Malformed suppression
meta · meta/malformed-suppression · default severity: error

What
  A suppression directive names no rule, or tries to suppress everything.

Why
  `//gofastr:allow(all)` is a hole, not a decision: it silently absorbs every
  rule added to the catalog afterwards, including ones written to catch the
  bug you are about to ship.

Fix
  Name each rule explicitly: `//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1401,GOFASTR1403)
  <reason>`.

Example
  ✗ //gofastr:allow(all) too noisy
  ✓ //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1401,GOFASTR1403) reviewed: static SQL, no user input

Docs
  gofastr docs contracts
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/contracts

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR0004) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR0004: warn   # or off

