=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1005

GOFASTR1005  Route method is not uppercase
routing · routing/non-uppercase-method · default severity: error

What
  A route is registered with a lowercase or mixed-case HTTP method.

Why
  ServeMux compares methods literally. `"get /x"` registers without complaint
  and then answers 405 to every real GET: a dead route that looks registered,
  with no boot-time error and no log line to find it by.

Fix
  Uppercase the method: "GET", "POST", "PUT", "PATCH", "DELETE".

Example
  ✗ r.Handle("post", "/orders", createOrder)
  ✓ r.Handle("POST", "/orders", createOrder)

Docs
  gofastr docs project-structure
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/project-structure

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1005) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1005: warn   # or off

