=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1902

GOFASTR1902  Mutating route with no access declaration
permissions · permissions/unguarded-mutation · default severity: warn

What
  A POST, PUT, PATCH, or DELETE route declares no middleware, group, or access
  rule.

Why
  A write endpoint that nothing guards is reachable by anyone who can reach
  the process. This is the single most common way an internal admin action
  becomes a public one, not by decision, but by a route added outside the
  group that carried the guard.

Fix
  Register it inside a guarded `app.Group(...)`, or attach access explicitly.
  If it is genuinely public (a webhook receiver, a health probe), say so with
  `//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1902) <why>`.

Example
  ✗ app.Delete("/admin/users/:id", deleteUser)
  ✓ admin := app.Group("/admin", access.Require("users:delete"))
  ✓ admin.Delete("/users/:id", deleteUser)

Docs
  gofastr docs access-control
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/access-control

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1902) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1902: warn   # or off

