=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1904

GOFASTR1904  Permission checked but never registered
permissions · permissions/unregistered-permission · default severity: error

What
  An access block, transition, or permission check names a capability the
  app's `RolePolicy.Register` list does not hold.

Why
  Permission names are strings, so a typo compiles. A check on a name nobody
  registered denies every role granted the intended capability, while the
  wildcard holder, usually the admin testing the screen, still passes, so it
  looks like it works. The rule runs once an app registers its capabilities,
  and checks each binary against the names registered in the packages it
  links.

Fix
  Correct the name to the registered capability, or add it to
  `RolePolicy.Register`. An untyped package-level `const` gives every check
  one spelling and fits both `access.Permission` and the `string` fields.

Example
  ✗ policy := access.NewRolePolicy()
  ✗ policy.Register("plans:write")
  ✗ _ = access.RequirePermission("plans:wirte")
  ✓ policy := access.NewRolePolicy()
  ✓ policy.Register("plans:write")
  ✓ _ = access.RequirePermission("plans:write")

Docs
  gofastr docs access-control
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/access-control

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1904) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1904: warn   # or off

