  "schema": 1,
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "GOFASTR1402",
      "slug": "security/form-without-csrf",
      "title": "POST form without a CSRF token",
      "capability": "security",
      "severity": "error",
      "summary": "A `\u003cform method=\"POST\"\u003e` is rendered without a CSRF input.",
      "why": "Any site the user visits can POST to yours with their cookies attached. Without a token the request is indistinguishable from one the user meant to make, which is how a page on another origin deletes their account.",
      "fix": "Render `CSRFInputFromCtx(ctx)` inside the form, or use `framework/ui` Form, which does it for you.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "bad": "\u003cform method=\"POST\" action=\"/delete\"\u003e",
          "good": "\u003cform method=\"POST\" action=\"/delete\"\u003e\n  {{ CSRFInputFromCtx(ctx) }}"
        }
      ],
      "doc": "security",
      "autofix": false,
      "docUrl": "https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/security",
      "docCommand": "gofastr docs security",
      "suppress": "//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1402) \u003creason\u003e"
    }
  ]
}

=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1403

GOFASTR1403  Untrusted value concatenated into HTML
security · security/html-concat · default severity: error

What
  `render.HTML` is called on a string built around a variable: a concatenation
  (on one line or several), a `fmt.Sprintf`/`Sprint`/`Sprintln` (a non-literal
  format counts), a `strings.Join`, or a local the function assigned one of
  these.

Why
  `render.HTML` means "this is already safe markup: do not escape it".
  Concatenating a variable into it hands the user's string straight to the
  browser as markup. That is stored XSS.

Fix
  Use `render.Text` for untrusted values (it escapes), or compose
  `core-ui/html` elements. If the concatenated half is genuinely a constant,
  annotate `//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1403) <why>`.

Example
  ✗ render.HTML("<h1>" + user.Name + "</h1>")
  ✓ html.Heading(html.HeadingConfig{Level: 1, Text: user.Name})

Docs
  gofastr docs security
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/security

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1403) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1403: warn   # or off

