=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1405

GOFASTR1405  Secret literal in source
security · security/hardcoded-secret · default severity: error

What
  A key, token, password, or secret is assigned from a string literal.

Why
  A committed secret is a leaked secret: it is in every clone, every fork, and
  the reflog after you delete it. Rotating is the only remedy, and rotation is
  expensive precisely when you discover this.

Fix
  Read it from the environment (`os.Getenv`) or `WithSecret`/`GOFASTR_SECRET`.
  Test fixtures and public constants are fine: annotate them `// not-a-secret:
  <why>`.

Example
  ✗ apiKey := "sk-live-9f3c2a1b8e7d6c5f4a3b2c1d"
  ✓ apiKey := os.Getenv("STRIPE_API_KEY")

Docs
  gofastr docs security
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/security

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1405) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1405: warn   # or off

