=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1410

GOFASTR1410  Local-filesystem Save with no folded-key refusal
security · security/folded-key-save · default severity: error

What
  A Save/Put/Write naming its stored object (a key/name parameter) on a type
  in the package with a BaseDir/Root/Dir field reaches a create, write or
  rename (os.OpenFile/Create/WriteFile/Rename, the same *os.Root methods, the
  atomicfile and fileperm write helpers) with no Fold-named refusal reachable
  from the method (strings.EqualFold is a comparison, not one).

Why
  On a case-insensitive or Unicode-normalization-insensitive filesystem (macOS
  APFS, most CIFS mounts), `tenanta/report.txt` and `TenantA/report.txt` are
  one file: the second save silently overwrites the first and each key's read
  returns the other writer's bytes (2026-09-05 red probe
  TestFoldedKeysDoNotAlias: battery/storage's local backend refuses the fold,
  core/upload's Save does not). A lexical key check cannot see the fold —
  only the filesystem's own resolution can.

Fix
  Refuse the folded key before anything is created or written, the
  battery/storage spelling: walk every path component, Lstat it as spelled,
  and os.SameFile-match the entry the parent directory actually holds; a
  byte-different name that matches is a fold, refuse it with ErrInvalidKey.

Example
  ✗ type LocalStorage struct{ baseDir string }
  ✗ 
  ✗ func (s *LocalStorage) Save(key string, r io.Reader) error {
  ✗ 	dst := filepath.Join(s.baseDir, key)
  ✗ 	tmp, _ := os.CreateTemp(filepath.Dir(dst), ".tmp-*")
  ✗ 	return os.Rename(tmp.Name(), dst)
  ✗ }
  ✓ func (ls *LocalStorage) Save(key string, r io.Reader) error {
  ✓ 	if err := ls.refuseFoldedKey(key, dstPath, root, ls.rootFor(root)); err != nil {
  ✓ 		return err // key collides with an object stored under a different spelling
  ✓ 	}
  ✓ 	return ls.finishSave(key, r)
  ✓ }

Docs
  gofastr docs security
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/security

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1410) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1410: warn   # or off

