=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1415

GOFASTR1415  A user-data table the erase and export planes never reach
security · security/erase-export-coverage · default severity: error

What
  A CREATE TABLE (or an ALTER TABLE … ADD COLUMN) in core/, framework/ or
  battery/ declares a user-identifying column (user_id, uid, owner, member_id,
  actor_id, subject, email, creator, principal, users, …) or a
  record-payload column (payload, body, data, content, snapshot, diff,
  task_json, config_json, an index document's text/fields/meta), and the same
  package has no `datexport.DataEraser` or no `datexport.DataExporter` whose
  Table (literal key or later field assignment) resolves to that table.

Why
  App.EraseUserData and App.ExportData reach the entity graph plus the tables
  registered in core/datexport, and nothing else. The 2026-10-27 bug bash
  found fourteen stores that create their own table and register neither (S9,
  S10, S20, S22–S32): battery/auth's OAuth token table keeps a live provider
  token for an erased user while every other auth table is erased; the outbox,
  webhook deliveries, search and semantic indexes, A2A tasks, idempotency
  bodies and fanout spill rows keep full copies of the user's records; the
  audit log is anonymized but never exported. Outside datexport itself only
  battery/auth and battery/queue declared anything.

Fix
  Declare the table to both planes from the package that creates it, the
  battery/auth erase.go + export.go pattern: a `datexport.DataEraser` keyed by
  the right identity (Column user_id, IdentityEmail for an email-keyed table,
  EraseAnonymize for a row that must be retained) and a
  `datexport.DataExporter`, re-registered against the configured table name
  when the store is built. When a short TTL or a non-user meaning is the
  reason not to, say so: `//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1415) <why>`.

Example
  ✗ func (s *TokenStore) ensure() error {
  ✗ 	_, err := s.db.Exec(fmt.Sprintf(`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS %s (user_id TEXT NOT NULL, token TEXT NOT NULL)`, s.table))
  ✗ 	return err
  ✗ }
  ✓ func (s *TokenStore) ensure() error {
  ✓ 	_, err := s.db.Exec(fmt.Sprintf(`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS %s (user_id TEXT NOT NULL, token TEXT NOT NULL)`, s.table))
  ✓ 	datexport.RegisterEraser(datexport.DataEraser{Name: "tokens", Table: s.table, Column: "user_id"})
  ✓ 	datexport.Register(datexport.DataExporter{Name: "tokens", Table: s.table, Columns: []string{"user_id", "token"}})
  ✓ 	return err
  ✓ }

Docs
  gofastr docs security
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/security

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1415) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1415: warn   # or off

