        {
          "bad": "func (s *TokenStore) ensure() error {\n\t_, err := s.db.Exec(fmt.Sprintf(`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS %s (user_id TEXT NOT NULL, token TEXT NOT NULL)`, s.table))\n\treturn err\n}",
          "good": "func (s *TokenStore) ensure() error {\n\t_, err := s.db.Exec(fmt.Sprintf(`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS %s (user_id TEXT NOT NULL, token TEXT NOT NULL)`, s.table))\n\tdatexport.RegisterEraser(datexport.DataEraser{Name: \"tokens\", Table: s.table, Column: \"user_id\"})\n\tdatexport.Register(datexport.DataExporter{Name: \"tokens\", Table: s.table, Columns: []string{\"user_id\", \"token\"}})\n\treturn err\n}"
        }
      ],
      "doc": "security",
      "autofix": false,
      "docUrl": "https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/security",
      "docCommand": "gofastr docs security",
      "suppress": "//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1415) \u003creason\u003e"
    }
  ]
}

=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1416

GOFASTR1416  An inline DDL constraint that never runs, or runs twice
security · security/inline-ddl-constraint · default severity: error

What
  (a) A column declared UNIQUE or REFERENCES inside a `CREATE TABLE IF NOT
  EXISTS` for a table the same package also declares as an entity (a
  schema.Field list whose names are all columns of that statement); (b) a
  column declared UNIQUE inside a CREATE TABLE, or marked `Unique: true` on a
  matching entity field, that a single-column `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX` also
  covers.

Why
  When the entity is declared, AutoMigrate creates the table first and the
  store's CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS is a no-op, so an inline constraint never
  exists: battery/auth's sessions.token UNIQUE never ran, every cookie lookup
  scanned the table and token uniqueness was not enforced (0550be96d). The
  fix's standalone CREATE UNIQUE INDEX then sat beside the inline UNIQUE and
  the entity field's Unique flag, so every session insert maintained two
  unique indexes on token (dbe11ba19).

Fix
  Declare the constraint once, where it runs whoever made the table: a
  standalone `CREATE [UNIQUE] INDEX IF NOT EXISTS` after the CREATE TABLE,
  with no UNIQUE inline and no Unique on the entity field beside it. A
  constraint that must stay inline says why: `//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1416)
  <why>`.

Example
  ✗ func (s *Store) ensure() error {
  ✗ 	_, err := s.db.Exec(`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL, token TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL)`)
  ✗ 	if err != nil {
  ✗ 		return err
  ✗ 	}
  ✗ 	_, err = s.db.Exec(`CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_sessions_token ON sessions (token)`)
  ✗ 	return err
  ✗ }
  ✓ func (s *Store) ensure() error {
  ✓ 	_, err := s.db.Exec(`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL, token TEXT NOT NULL)`)
  ✓ 	if err != nil {
  ✓ 		return err
  ✓ 	}
  ✓ 	_, err = s.db.Exec(`CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_sessions_token ON sessions (token)`)
  ✓ 	return err
  ✓ }

Docs
  gofastr docs security
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/security

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1416) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1416: warn   # or off

