=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1417

GOFASTR1417  A status UPDATE that skips the stamps its siblings write
security · security/status-update-skips-stamps · default severity: warn

What
  An `UPDATE <table> SET status = …` writes none of the stamp columns
  (updated_at, last_error, finished_at, completed_at, failed_at, …) while at
  least two other status UPDATEs on the same table in the same package all
  write one. Tables resolve the way GOFASTR1415 resolves them (literal,
  constant, receiver field, quoting wrapper, a method returning the name).

Why
  When every transition of a table records when and why the row moved and one
  does not, the row lists with an earlier transition's timestamp and error,
  and nobody can tell which path moved it. battery/queue's lease-expiry
  dead-letter sweep set status='failed' and nothing else while claim, Ack,
  Nack, release and Replay all wrote updated_at (Nack last_error too), so
  ListJobs("failed") showed a worker that died holding its claim as an earlier
  attempt's handler error (04ac2e5e6).

Fix
  Write the stamps the sibling transitions write, with a reason a reader can
  tell apart (the queue's leaseExpiredError). A transition that must keep the
  earlier stamp on purpose says so: `//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1417) <why>`.

Example
  ✗ func (q *Queue) ack(id string) {
  ✗ 	q.db.Exec(`UPDATE jobs SET status='done', updated_at=$1 WHERE id=$2`, now(), id)
  ✗ }
  ✗ 
  ✗ func (q *Queue) nack(id, why string) {
  ✗ 	q.db.Exec(`UPDATE jobs SET status='failed', updated_at=$1, last_error=$2 WHERE id=$3`, now(), why, id)
  ✗ }
  ✗ 
  ✗ func (q *Queue) sweep(id string) {
  ✗ 	q.db.Exec(`UPDATE jobs SET status='failed' WHERE id=$1`, id)
  ✗ }
  ✓ func (q *Queue) ack(id string) {
  ✓ 	q.db.Exec(`UPDATE jobs SET status='done', updated_at=$1 WHERE id=$2`, now(), id)
  ✓ }
  ✓ 
  ✓ func (q *Queue) nack(id, why string) {
  ✓ 	q.db.Exec(`UPDATE jobs SET status='failed', updated_at=$1, last_error=$2 WHERE id=$3`, now(), why, id)
  ✓ }
  ✓ 
  ✓ func (q *Queue) sweep(id string) {
  ✓ 	q.db.Exec(`UPDATE jobs SET status='failed', updated_at=$1, last_error=$2 WHERE id=$3`, now(), "lease expired", id)
  ✓ }

Docs
  gofastr docs security
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/security

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1417) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1417: warn   # or off

