=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1418

GOFASTR1418  A hand-written primary key that accepts NULL
security · security/nullable-primary-key · default severity: error

What
  A CREATE TABLE string (a literal, a fmt.Sprintf format or a concatenation)
  declares a primary key column without NOT NULL: inline (`id TEXT PRIMARY
  KEY`) or through a table-level `PRIMARY KEY (a, b)` whose column lacks it. A
  column or table named through a verb or an operand is read as that
  expression. Quiet on a lone `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY` (SQLite's rowid) and a
  SERIAL key, which the engine fills itself, on DDL assembled piece by piece
  (a strings.Builder, a joined slice), on .sql files, and on _test.go files.

Why
  SQLite lets NULL into every primary key column but a lone INTEGER one, any
  number of times; Postgres refuses the row. A store that reads or deletes by
  key never finds such a row, so it cannot be fetched, updated, erased or
  exported, and the two engines disagree about which inserts succeed.
  AutoMigrate writes NOT NULL on the keys it creates; about thirty
  hand-written framework, battery and core tables (audit, outbox, queue,
  webhook, idempotency, feature flags, A2A, the auth stores) did not.

Fix
  Write NOT NULL on every primary key column: `id TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL`,
  and NOT NULL on each column a table-level PRIMARY KEY names. A table that
  already exists keeps the definition it was created with. A key that is
  filled by the engine in a way the rule cannot see says so:
  `//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1418) <why>`.

Example
  ✗ func (s *Store) ensure() error {
  ✗ 	_, err := s.db.Exec(`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS flags (key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, enabled BOOLEAN NOT NULL)`)
  ✗ 	return err
  ✗ }
  ✓ func (s *Store) ensure() error {
  ✓ 	_, err := s.db.Exec(`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS flags (key TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL, enabled BOOLEAN NOT NULL)`)
  ✓ 	return err
  ✓ }

Docs
  gofastr docs security
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/security

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1418) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1418: warn   # or off

