=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1601

GOFASTR1601  Write result discarded
data · data/ignored-exec · default severity: error

What
  The result and error of a `db.Exec` are both dropped: assigned to `_`, or
  the call stands alone as a statement (plain, deferred or in a goroutine).

Why
  The write may not have happened. A constraint violation, a closed
  connection, a read-only replica: all of them return an error here and none
  of them are visible. The request returns 200 and the data is gone.

Fix
  Handle the error, or state that you mean it: `// best-effort: <why>` on the
  line or just above it.

Example
  ✗ _, _ = db.Exec("DELETE FROM sessions WHERE id = $1", id)
  ✓ if _, err := db.Exec("DELETE FROM sessions WHERE id = $1", id); err != nil {
  ✓     return fmt.Errorf("revoke session: %w", err)
  ✓ }

Example
  ✗ db.Exec(`INSERT INTO posts (id, title) VALUES ('p1', 'Hello')`)
  ✓ if _, err := db.Exec(`INSERT INTO posts (id, title) VALUES ('p1', 'Hello')`); err != nil {
  ✓     return fmt.Errorf("seed: %w", err)
  ✓ }

Docs
  gofastr docs hooks-and-transactions
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/hooks-and-transactions

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1601) <reason>

Relax project-wide
