=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1702

GOFASTR1702  Entity exposed anonymously
entities · entities/public-entity · default severity: warn

What
  An entity sets Public, opting out of the session requirement on every
  operation.

Why
  Auto-CRUD is secure by default: every operation requires a session. Public
  removes that for reads *and writes*, so anyone on the internet can create
  and delete rows unless another gate stops them. That is sometimes exactly
  right, and it should always be deliberate.

Fix
  Confirm the entity is genuinely public data. If only reads should be, keep
  Public off and grant read access through `access:` permissions instead.

Example
  ✗ app.Entity("invoices", entity.EntityConfig{Exposure: &entity.ExposureConfig{Public: true}})
  ✓ app.Entity("invoices", entity.EntityConfig{Exposure: &entity.ExposureConfig{Access: entity.AccessControl{Read: "invoices:read"}}})

Docs
  gofastr docs access-control
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/access-control

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1702) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1702: warn   # or off

