      "docCommand": "gofastr docs project-structure",
      "suppress": "//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1301) \u003creason\u003e"
    }
  ]
}

=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1302

GOFASTR1302  Forbidden import edge
architecture · architecture/forbidden-import · default severity: error

What
  An import matches a `contracts.architecture.forbid` entry.

Why
  Some edges are banned for reasons no layer ordering expresses: a package
  that must stay dependency-free so it can be vendored, or a decoder set that
  must not be linked into every binary. The ban is only real if something
  checks it.

Fix
  Remove the import, or route it through the seam the forbid rule's reason
  names.

Example
  ✗ import "example.com/app/internal/store" // forbid: ui -> store
  ✓ import "example.com/app/internal/service" // the seam the forbid entry names

Docs
  gofastr docs project-structure
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/project-structure

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1302) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1302: warn   # or off

