=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1802

GOFASTR1802  Full page reload used as navigation
rendering · rendering/hard-navigation · default severity: error

What
  Client code assigns `location.href` or calls `location.reload()`.

Why
  It throws away the whole document to change one thing: scroll position,
  focus, form state, and every open island go with it. It also re-downloads
  and re-parses the CSS and runtime that were already there. Cross-page
  navigation in GoFastr is client-side with a cache.

Fix
  Let the runtime navigate, a plain `<a href>` is intercepted, or return
  `X-Gofastr-Location` from the server to redirect after an action.

Example
  ✗ location.href = '/orders'
  ✓ <a href="/orders">Orders</a>  <!-- the runtime intercepts it -->

Docs
  gofastr docs runtime-contract
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/runtime-contract

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1802) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1802: warn   # or off

