=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1804

GOFASTR1804  Inline style attribute
rendering · rendering/inline-style · default severity: error

What
  Markup carries a `style="…"` attribute.

Why
  Inline styles beat every stylesheet rule, so the component they are applied
  to can no longer be restyled or themed, including by the dark-mode tokens.
  They are also blocked outright under a strict Content-Security-Policy.

Fix
  Use the component's config or a `core-ui/style` token. A value that
  genuinely varies per render belongs in a CSS custom property the component
  reads.

Example
  ✗ html.Raw(`<div style="margin-top: 12px">…</div>`)
  ✓ ui.Stack(ui.StackConfig{Gap: "md"}, children...)

Docs
  gofastr docs theming
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/theming

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1804) <reason>

Relax project-wide
