=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1805

GOFASTR1805  Inline script block
rendering · rendering/inline-script · default severity: error

What
  Markup emits a `<script>` block with a body rather than a `src`.

Why
  The framework's default Content-Security-Policy is `default-src 'self'` with
  no `unsafe-inline`, so the browser refuses to execute the block. Nothing
  fails at build or render time: the page ships, the script silently never
  runs, and whatever it wired up is simply missing in production while working
  in any environment with a laxer policy.

Fix
  Move the body to a file and reference it: `<script src="/static/x.js">`. For
  behaviour attached to server-rendered markup, prefer the runtime's
  `data-cui-*` hydration over a script tag at all: see `gofastr docs
  runtime-contract`.

Example
  ✗ html.Raw(`<script>document.title = "Orders"</script>`)
  ✓ html.Raw(`<script src="/static/orders.js" defer></script>`)

Docs
  gofastr docs security
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/security

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1805) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1805: warn   # or off

