=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1812

GOFASTR1812  @media width that is not a theme breakpoint
rendering · rendering/raw-media-width · default severity: error

What
  An @media query in a *.style.css tests min-width, max-width or width against
  a raw length instead of a custom media name.

Why
  Breakpoints are theme tokens. A raw 768px drifts from the theme the day the
  breakpoint moves, and two sheets writing 767px and 768px disagree about
  which layout a window between them gets. var() is invalid in a media query,
  so the owned-style compiler expands custom media names (--above-md,
  --below-lg) against the running theme's breakpoints instead. Raw widths stay
  legal in @container, which measures a container, not the viewport.

Fix
  Write @media (--above-md) or (--below-lg); combine a custom medium with
  other features using `and`, e.g. (--above-md) and (hover: hover).

Example
  ✗ @media (min-width: 768px) { .board { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  ✓ @media (--above-md) { .board { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }

Docs
  gofastr docs contracts
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/contracts

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1812) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1812: warn   # or off

