=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1813

GOFASTR1813  Animation with no reduced-motion block
rendering · rendering/animation-without-reduced-motion · default severity: warn

What
  A rule in a *.style.css sets animation or animation-name, and no @media
  (--reduced-motion) block holds a rule for the same selector.

Why
  Motion can trigger nausea and vestibular symptoms, and WCAG 2.3.3 asks that
  non-essential animation can be turned off. The owned-style compiler expands
  (--reduced-motion) to prefers-reduced-motion: reduce; the check looks for a
  rule with the same selector inside such a block. It is a warning because
  some animation is essential (a progress indicator), which the check cannot
  tell.

Fix
  Add @media (--reduced-motion) { <the same selector> { animation: none; } },
  or a slower, non-moving alternative.

Example
  ✗ .pulse { animation: pulse 1s infinite; }
  ✓ .pulse { animation: pulse 1s infinite; }
  ✓ @media (--reduced-motion) { .pulse { animation: none; } }

Docs
  gofastr docs accessibility
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/accessibility

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1813) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1813: warn   # or off

