=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1818

GOFASTR1818  Screen or layout style used outside its owner's package
rendering · rendering/owned-style-outside-owner · default severity: error

What
  A style handle attached with LayoutSpec.Style or Screen.WithStyle is used
  (its class methods called) in a package that is neither the handle's own nor
  the one that attaches it.

Why
  A layout's or screen's style compiles into an @scope bound to that owner's
  root, so its class names mean something only inside that element. Called
  from another package (a shared component, another screen), a method returns
  a class that matches nothing when the markup renders outside the owner, or
  matches by accident when it happens to land inside, so the styling depends
  on where the caller is rendered today. The handle must be named directly
  (Style, <Owner>Style, or pkg.Style) for the rule to see it; a handle copied
  into a variable is not traced.

Fix
  Keep a screen's or layout's classes in the style's own package (where its
  .style.css sits) or the one that attaches it. Markup another package renders
  is a component: give it its own <name>.style.css and scope its root with
  Style.Scope.

Example
  ✗ // package widgets; board.Style is attached by Screen.WithStyle in package board
  ✗ func lane() string { return board.Style.Column() }
  ✓ // package widgets, with its own widgets/lane.style.css
  ✓ func lane(content render.HTML) render.HTML { return Style.Scope(content) }

Docs
  gofastr docs layouts
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/layouts

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1818) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1818: warn   # or off

