=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1824

GOFASTR1824  Kit CSS pins a physical side where a reading-direction one exists
rendering · rendering/physical-side · default severity: error

What
  Design-system CSS names left or right: a left/right offset, a margin,
  padding, scroll margin or border on one side, a corner radius, text-align,
  float or clear set to left or right, a background position on a side with no
  `:dir(rtl)` mirror in the file, or a four-value margin, padding, inset or
  border shorthand whose left and right differ. left: 50% and right: 50%
  (centring), auto, and a line that is itself a :dir() override pass. Dev
  tooling (framework/dev) is exempt.

Why
  A page renders <html dir="rtl"> for Arabic, Hebrew, Persian and the other
  right-to-left scripts. Logical properties follow that direction on their
  own; a physical one keeps the sidebar border, the list indent, the toast
  corner and the select chevron on the left-to-right side, so the kit looks
  broken to every right-to-left reader.

Fix
  Write the logical property: inset-inline-start/end for left/right,
  margin-inline-start, padding-inline-end, border-inline-end,
  border-start-start-radius, text-align: start, float: inline-start,
  padding-block plus padding-inline for an asymmetric shorthand. A value with
  no logical spelling (a background position, a translateX travel) gets a
  :dir(rtl) override beside it. A side that must stay physical carries
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1824) with the reason.

Example
  ✗ border-right: var(--stroke-thin, 1px) solid var(--color-border); padding-left: var(--spacing-lg, 16px); text-align: left;
  ✓ border-inline-end: var(--stroke-thin, 1px) solid var(--color-border); padding-inline-start: var(--spacing-lg, 16px); text-align: start;

Docs
  gofastr docs i18n
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/i18n

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1824) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1824: warn   # or off

