=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1825

GOFASTR1825  Owned style holds a statement at-rule
rendering · rendering/owned-statement-at-rule · default severity: error

What
  A *.style.css holds a statement at-rule other than @layer: @import,
  @charset, @namespace.

Why
  These at-rules count only at the top of a stylesheet, before every other
  rule. An owned sheet compiles into app.css after the kit's rules, and a
  scoped one inside its @scope block, so the browser ignores them: the font or
  sheet an @import names never loads, and nothing on the page says so.

Fix
  Load web fonts through the theme (style.FontFaceCSS) and write the rules you
  meant to import in the owned sheet itself.

Example
  ✗ @import url(fonts.css);
  ✗ .lane { order: 1; }
  ✓ .lane { order: 1; }

Docs
  gofastr docs theming
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/theming

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1825) <reason>

Relax project-wide
