=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1826

GOFASTR1826  Kit CSS reverses a flex row or column, so reading order and visual order disagree
rendering · rendering/flex-reverse · default severity: error

What
  Design-system CSS sets flex-direction (or the flex-flow shorthand) to
  row-reverse or column-reverse, in a stylesheet or a Set("flex-direction",
  …) pair. Dev tooling (framework/dev) is exempt.

Why
  A reversed flex container paints its children against their document order.
  A screen reader, the Tab key and a radio group's own arrow keys follow the
  document, so they move the other way from what the reader sees (WCAG 1.3.2
  and 2.4.3). ui.RatingInput rendered its stars Max..1 for a sibling cascade
  and flipped them back with row-reverse: ArrowRight went to the lower star.

Fix
  Render the children in the order they read and lay them out forward; a fill
  or highlight that needs "every earlier sibling" selects it with :has() over
  a later one (the Rating sheet's spelling). A reversed box whose children
  carry no order of their own (a purely decorative stack) carries
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1826) with the reason.

Example
  ✗ display: inline-flex; flex-direction: row-reverse; justify-content: flex-end;
  ✓ display: inline-flex; /* children render 1..N; the fill reads :has() */

Docs
  gofastr docs accessibility
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/accessibility

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1826) <reason>

Relax project-wide
