=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1203

GOFASTR1203  Landmark without a name
accessibility · accessibility/unnamed-landmark · default severity: error

What
  A nav, section, aside, or group landmark has no accessible name or role.

Why
  Screen-reader users navigate by landmark. Three `<nav>` elements that all
  announce as "navigation" are worse than one, because now the user has to
  enter each to find out which is which.

Fix
  Set Label ("Main", "Footer") or LabelledBy pointing at a heading id. If it
  is not a landmark, use a plain Div.

Example
  ✗ html.Nav(html.NavConfig{}, links...)
  ✓ html.Nav(html.NavConfig{Label: "Primary"}, links...)

Docs
  gofastr docs accessibility
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/accessibility

