=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1205

GOFASTR1205  Heading without an explicit level
accessibility · accessibility/implicit-heading-level · default severity: error

What
  An `html.Heading` omits Level.

Why
  Heading levels form the page outline screen-reader users navigate by.
  Picking a level to get the font size you want breaks that outline: one h1,
  no skipped levels. Font size is a styling concern.

Fix
  Set Level explicitly to the level the outline needs, and size it with the
  design system's tokens.

Example
  ✗ html.Heading(html.HeadingConfig{}, html.Text("Orders"))
  ✓ html.Heading(html.HeadingConfig{Level: 2}, html.Text("Orders"))

Docs
  gofastr docs accessibility
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/accessibility

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1205) <reason>

Relax project-wide
