  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "GOFASTR1205",
      "slug": "accessibility/implicit-heading-level",
      "title": "Heading without an explicit level",
      "capability": "accessibility",
      "severity": "error",
      "summary": "An `html.Heading` omits Level.",
      "why": "Heading levels form the page outline screen-reader users navigate by. Picking a level to get the font size you want breaks that outline: one h1, no skipped levels. Font size is a styling concern.",
      "fix": "Set Level explicitly to the level the outline needs, and size it with the design system's tokens.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "bad": "html.Heading(html.HeadingConfig{}, html.Text(\"Orders\"))",
          "good": "html.Heading(html.HeadingConfig{Level: 2}, html.Text(\"Orders\"))"
        }
      ],
      "doc": "accessibility",
      "autofix": false,
      "docUrl": "https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/accessibility",
      "docCommand": "gofastr docs accessibility",
      "suppress": "//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1205) \u003creason\u003e"
    }
  ]
}

=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1206

GOFASTR1206  Element missing required metadata
accessibility · accessibility/missing-element-metadata · default severity: error

What
  A core-ui/html element omits a field the accessibility contract requires.

Why
  Each of these fields exists because assistive technology has no way to infer
  it: an abbreviation's expansion, a time element's machine-readable value, a
  media source's type.

Fix
  Fill in the field named in the message. `gofastr docs accessibility` lists
  the requirement per element.

Example
  ✗ html.Time(html.TimeConfig{}, html.Text("yesterday"))
  ✓ html.Time(html.TimeConfig{Datetime: "2026-08-03"}, html.Text("yesterday"))

Docs
  gofastr docs accessibility
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/accessibility

Suppress once
