=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1104

GOFASTR1104  Line coverage below the configured floor
testing · testing/coverage-below-minimum · default severity: error

What
  The coverage profile reports less than the configured minimum.

Why
  A floor that drifts downward one merge at a time is not a floor. This check
  exists to make the drift a build failure at the moment it happens, rather
  than a number someone notices a quarter later.

Fix
  Add tests, or lower `contracts.coverage.minimum` deliberately: the change
  will be visible in review.

Example
  ✗ contracts:
  ✗   coverage:
  ✗     minimum: 90   # profile reports 71%
  ✓ contracts:
  ✓   coverage:
  ✓     minimum: 70   # lowered deliberately, visible in review

Docs
  gofastr docs contracts
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/contracts

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1104) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1104: warn   # or off

