=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1105

GOFASTR1105  Test disabled without a stated boundary
testing · testing/disabled-test · default severity: error

What
  A `t.Skip` hides missing coverage rather than marking a lane boundary.

Why
  `t.Skip("TODO")` reports as a pass. The suite stays green while the
  behaviour it claims to cover is unverified: the most expensive kind of
  green.

Fix
  Fix the test, delete it, or state the boundary: an explicit
  `testing.Short()` guard, an environment-capability skip, or
  `//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1105) <why>`.

Example
  ✗ t.Skip("not yet implemented")
  ✓ if testing.Short() {
  ✓     t.Skip("chromedp suite: -short")
  ✓ }

Docs
  gofastr docs testkit
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/testkit

Suppress once
