=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1106

GOFASTR1106  No semantic-coverage manifest
testing · testing/no-coverage-manifest · default severity: info

What
  `.gofastr/semantic-coverage.json` does not exist, so the semantic-coverage
  checks could not run.

Why
  Absence is reported rather than enforced: a fresh clone has never run its
  tests, and walling off first verify behind a full test run would teach the
  wrong lesson. Drift (a manifest that exists but misses a route) is the
  failure worth catching: that is GOFASTR1101.

Fix
  Run `go test ./...` once. Every `framework.TestHarness` request writes to
  the manifest from then on.

Example
  ✗ # .gofastr/semantic-coverage.json absent: the testing rules check nothing
  ✓ go test ./...   # every TestHarness request records into the manifest

Docs
  gofastr docs testkit
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/testkit

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1106) <reason>

Relax project-wide
