=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1107

GOFASTR1107  Lifecycle hook never ran
testing · testing/hook-not-fired · default severity: warn

What
  A registered entity lifecycle hook never fired during the recorded test run.

Why
  This is the quietest way a feature stops working. The hook is still
  registered, the handler it decorates still has coverage, and the suite is
  still green, but the behaviour the hook adds (the audit row, the derived
  column, the cache bust) has not happened once. Nothing in a line-coverage
  report can tell you that.

Fix
  Exercise the operation the hook is attached to through the HTTP surface: a
  `framework.TestHarness` request to the entity's create/update/delete
  endpoint fires it and records it.

Example: registered but never exercised
  ✗ framework.OnBeforeCreate[Post](app, `posts`, stampSlug)
  ✗ // nothing in the suite ever POSTs /posts, so stampSlug has never run
  ✓ framework.OnBeforeCreate[Post](app, `posts`, stampSlug)
  ✓ // ta.Post(`/posts`, Post{Title: `x`}).AssertStatus(t, 201)

Docs
  gofastr docs hooks-and-transactions
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/hooks-and-transactions

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1107) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1107: warn   # or off

=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1107 --json
{
  "schema": 1,
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "GOFASTR1107",
      "slug": "testing/hook-not-fired",
      "title": "Lifecycle hook never ran",
      "capability": "testing",
      "severity": "warn",
      "summary": "A registered entity lifecycle hook never fired during the recorded test run.",
      "why": "This is the quietest way a feature stops working. The hook is still registered, the handler it decorates still has coverage, and the suite is still green, but the behaviour the hook adds (the audit row, the derived column, the cache bust) has not happened once. Nothing in a line-coverage report can tell you that.",
      "fix": "Exercise the operation the hook is attached to through the HTTP surface: a `framework.TestHarness` request to the entity's create/update/delete endpoint fires it and records it.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "caption": "registered but never exercised",
          "bad": "framework.OnBeforeCreate[Post](app, `posts`, stampSlug)\n// nothing in the suite ever POSTs /posts, so stampSlug has never run",
          "good": "framework.OnBeforeCreate[Post](app, `posts`, stampSlug)\n// ta.Post(`/posts`, Post{Title: `x`}).AssertStatus(t, 201)"
        }
      ],
      "doc": "hooks-and-transactions",
      "autofix": false,
      "docUrl": "https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/hooks-and-transactions",
      "docCommand": "gofastr docs hooks-and-transactions",
      "suppress": "//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1107) \u003creason\u003e"
    }
  ]
}

=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR1108

GOFASTR1108  Event subscriber never ran
testing · testing/event-subscriber-not-exercised · default severity: warn

What
  A handler is subscribed to an event type that was never published during the
  recorded test run.

Why
  A subscriber is invisible until its event fires. Nothing calls it directly,
  so it has no callers to follow and no failing test to notice: the
  notification is simply never sent, the projection never updated, and the
  suite stays green. Renaming the event type on the emitting side breaks it
  silently and identically.

Fix
  Emit the event in a test, usually by exercising the operation that publishes
  it, so the subscriber runs at least once. If it is only ever emitted by
  another service, say so with a suppression.

Example: subscribed to a type nothing publishes
  ✗ bus.On(`order.place`, sendReceipt) // the emitter publishes `order.placed`; sendReceipt has never run
  ✓ bus.On(`order.placed`, sendReceipt) // a checkout test emits order.placed, so the subscriber runs

Docs
  gofastr docs events
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/events

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR1108) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR1108: warn   # or off

