=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR2002

GOFASTR2002  Hand-rolled subsystem a battery provides
ai · ai/handrolled-battery · default severity: warn

What
  Code implements auth, email, queueing, storage, or scheduling directly.

Why
  These are the subsystems where a from-scratch version is 80% right and the
  missing 20% is the security-relevant part: session rotation, retry backoff,
  signed URLs. The batteries are wired into the app lifecycle, the audit log,
  and the test harness; a local one is not.

Fix
  Register the battery instead: `gofastr docs overview` lists them. Batteries
  are composable: keep your custom logic in a hook.

Example
  ✗ hash, _ := bcrypt.GenerateFromPassword(pw, bcrypt.DefaultCost) // hand-rolled auth
  ✓ app.Use(auth.New(auth.Config{})) // battery/auth

Docs
  gofastr docs overview
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/overview

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR2002) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR2002: warn   # or off

