=== gofastr verify --explain GOFASTR2003

GOFASTR2003  Raw SQL against an entity's table
ai · ai/raw-sql-over-repository · default severity: info

What
  A raw query targets a table that has a declared entity and a generated
  repository.

Why
  Raw SQL bypasses every scoping rule the entity declares: soft delete, tenant
  filter, owner field. A query written before those existed keeps returning
  rows they were added to hide.

Fix
  Use the entity's typed repository, which applies the scoping. Raw SQL is
  fine for reporting and migrations: annotate those
  `//gofastr:allow(GOFASTR2003) <why>`.

Example
  ✗ db.Query("SELECT * FROM invoices WHERE user_id = ?", uid) // invoices is a declared entity
  ✓ repo.List(ctx, filter) // the generated repository applies the scoping

Docs
  gofastr docs query-dsl
  https://donaldmurillo.github.io/gofastr/docs/query-dsl

Suppress once
  //gofastr:allow(GOFASTR2003) <reason>

Relax project-wide
  contracts:
    rules:
      GOFASTR2003: warn   # or off

